BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:the-start-of-hanukkah-20261204@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261204
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261205
SUMMARY:The Start of Hanukkah
DESCRIPTION:Hanukkah is an eight-night festival that begins on 25 Kislev an
 d marks the rededication of the Second Temple in Jerusalem after the Macca
 bean revolt. A day in the Hebrew calendar begins at sundown\, so the first
  candle is lit on the evening the festival opens — the date listed here 
 — while 25 Kislev itself is the Gregorian day that follows. It was for m
 ost of its history a minor holiday\; its prominence in American life is a 
 nineteenth- and twentieth-century development\, and its nearness to Decemb
 er 25 has a good deal to do with that.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holi
 day/the-start-of-hanukkah/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/the-start-of-hanukkah/
CATEGORIES:Celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
